§ `Library Lending Act`

-- A small bespoke act for the TNR demo: definitions (DECLARE / MEANS),
-- a prohibition that exercises the negative-universal rewrite, and a
-- pair of chained obligations (PARTY / MUST / HENCE / LEST).

§§ `Definitions`

DECLARE Borrower HAS
    Name IS A STRING

DECLARE Book HAS
    Title              IS A STRING
    `Replacement cost` IS A NUMBER

`The loan period in days` MEANS 28

`The late fee per day` MEANS 0.50

ASSUME `the borrower` IS A Borrower

ASSUME `the borrower is a member of the library` IS A BOOLEAN
ASSUME `the borrower has unpaid fines exceeding ten dollars` IS A BOOLEAN
ASSUME `the borrower has been banned by the head librarian` IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `Eligibility`

DECIDE `the borrower must not borrow a book`
IF  NOT `the borrower is a member of the library`
    OR  `the borrower has unpaid fines exceeding ten dollars`
    OR  `the borrower has been banned by the head librarian`

§§ `Obligations`

DECLARE `Loan event` IS ONE OF
    `return the book`
        HAS `Returned copy` IS A Book
    `pay the accrued late fee`
        HAS `Amount paid` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN borrowed IS A Book
`The duty to return` MEANS
    PARTY `the borrower`
    MUST  `return the book` `Returned copy`
              PROVIDED `Returned copy`'s Title EQUALS borrowed's Title
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  `The duty to pay the late fee` borrowed

GIVEN borrowed IS A Book
`The duty to pay the late fee` MEANS
    PARTY `the borrower`
    MUST  `pay the accrued late fee` `Amount paid`
              PROVIDED `Amount paid` AT LEAST `The late fee per day`
    HENCE FULFILLED
